--TEST--
a `discover` glob whose `*` is not one whole path segment does not compile — `rule:programs/autoload`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A typo that silently discovers nothing is the worst outcome on offer, so a
// glob's own shape is checked rather than its yield: exactly one `*`,
// occupying a whole path segment. Both malformed spellings below are
// reported from the same run, and nothing here names a discovered class —
// the shape is refused before any directory is scanned.
require './bootstrap.nvs';
--FILE bootstrap.nvs--
<?nvs
autoload discover './plugin-*/src';
autoload discover './*/*/src';
--FILE Plugin/src/Tool.nvs--
<?nvs
namespace Plugin;

// What a well-formed './*/src' would have found.
class Tool
{
    public static function from(): string
    {
        return "the discovered root";
    }
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0318]: `./plugin-*/src` is not a discovery glob
%A
error[E0318]: `./*/*/src` holds more than one `*`
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
